.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Lineweaver and Burk (1934) inverted the Michaelis-Menten equation into a straight line, 1/v = (K_m/V_{max})(1/[S]) + 1/V_{max}, so V_{max} and K_m could be read off the intercept and slope. fit_lineweaver_burk does exactly that fit on noisy initial-rate data. The second panel shows the method&#x27;s well-known weakness: the same small relative noise becomes a large scatter at the low-[S] (large 1/[S]) end, which dominates the fitted line.">

